{"step_index":910,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T11:55:53Z","input_tokens":96621,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1969,"content":"The **Quant Engine** is the brain that prevents the #1 cause of bot death: **using the same trading strategy in every market condition**. \n\nA standard bot is like a car driving 100 km/h in bright sunshine, heavy rain, thick fog, and black ice. Eventually, it crashes. The Quant Engine constantly scans the road surface and changes the car’s tires, speed, and braking system automatically.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Market Regime Classification (Detecting the \"Weather\")\nRather than guessing where price goes, the engine classifies the market into **4 mathematical states** using volatility ($\\sigma$), spread width, and price velocity:\n\n```\n                  ┌─────────────── Market Regimes ───────────────┐\n                  │                                              │\n    [CALM]        │ Low volatility (<1.2%), tight spread, stable │ Strategy: Mean Reversion / Grid\n    [TRENDING]    │ Directional volume push, sustained momentum  │ Strategy: Breakout / Trend-Following\n    [JITTERY]     │ Erratic chop, sudden spikes, false breakouts │ Strategy: Sit in Cash / Cut Size 50%\n    [CRASH]       │ Bids vanish, spread explodes, heavy selloff  │ Strategy: 100% Cash / Circuit Breaker\n```\n\n* **Why this matters**: A trend-following strategy gets chopped to pieces in a `CALM` or `JITTERY` market. A grid bot gets wiped out in a `TRENDING` or `CRASH` market. The Quant Engine swaps strategies before taking the trade.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Order Book Imbalance (OBI — Reading Microstructure)\nBefore touching price charts, the engine inspects the **top of the order book** (the bids and asks sitting on the exchange waiting to get filled):\n\n$$\\text{OBI} = \\frac{\\text{Volume}_{\\text{Bids}} - \\text{Volume}_{\\text{Asks}}}{\\text{Volume}_{\\text{Bids}} + \\text{Volume}_{\\text{Asks}}}$$\n\n* **$\\text{OBI} > +0.35$ (Heavy Buying Wall)**: More capital is bidding to buy than sell. Price has upward pressure.\n* **$\\text{OBI} < -0.35$ (Heavy Selling Wall)**: Asks outnumber bids. Downward pre\n<truncated 307 bytes>\ny Criterion**, which calculates the mathematically optimal bet size:\n\n$$f^* = \\frac{b \\cdot p - (1 - p)}{b}$$\n\n*(where $p = \\text{win rate}$, $b = \\text{reward-to-risk ratio}$)*\n\n* **Why Full Kelly Kills Accounts**: Full Kelly assumes normal distributions. Crypto has \"fat tails\" (black swan dumps). \n* **The Solution — Quarter-Kelly ($f^* / 4$)**: We size down to 25% of theoretical Kelly:\n  * In a high-confidence `TRENDING` regime with $+0.50$ OBI $\\to$ Allocates up to $8\\%\\text{--}12\\%$ of bankroll.\n  * In a `JITTERY` regime $\\to$ Scales down to $2\\%\\text{--}3\\%$ or zero.\n\n---\n\n### 4. The 15% Handbrake (High-Water Mark Circuit Breaker)\nThis is the uncompromised fail-safe:\n\n$$\\text{Drawdown} = \\frac{\\text{Peak Balance (High-Water Mark)} - \\text{Current Balance}}{\\text{Peak Balance}}$$\n\n```\n  $5,000 (Peak HWM)\n     │\n     ▼ -15% Drawdown Level ($4,250)\n  ───┼────────────────────────────────────────── [CIRCUIT BREAKER HARD TRIP]\n     │                                            • Closes all open inventory\n     │                                            • Freezes new order placement\n     │                                            • Requires human override to reset\n```\n\n* **Checked BEFORE Every Order**: Most bots blow up because they keep trading during an exchange outage, flash depeg, or cascading liquidation.\n* If drawdown ever touches $15\\%$, the circuit breaker immediately locks the engine in emergency halt. No algorithm is permitted to risk capital past that line.\n\n---\n\n### How to See It Live\nIn your [deployed dashboard](https://grok-bot-dashboard.pages.dev) (or [local](http://localhost:5173)):\n1. Toggle the header switch to **\"Quant Regime\"**.\n2. Notice the **Order Book Imbalance** meter fluctuate between green (Bids) and red (Asks).\n3. Observe how the active regime badge transitions (`CALM` $\\leftrightarrow$ `TRENDING` $\\leftrightarrow$ `JITTERY`) and directly alters position sizes in the trade log.","thinking":"Quant engine... it crunches numbers, fast. It takes data, does the math. It aims to figure out stuff, using special ways to simplify.\n\n\nQuant engine... it crunches numbers, fast. It takes data, does the math. It aims to figure out stuff, using special ways to simplify.\n\nMarket regime detection classifies trading environments into distinct states: CALM, TRENDING, JITTERY, and CRASH, leveraging volatility, spread, and order book imbalance. Specifically, order book imbalance (OBI) quantifies the directional pressure in the order book; it's calculated and then used for market regime classification. Different regimes suggest optimal trading strategies—mean reversion in CALM, trend following in TRENDING, cash positions or ultra-tight stops for JITTERY, and short-only or cash in CRASH/FREEFALL.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
