g fees and slippage on paper, it will 100% lose real money.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: The Benchmark Challenge\nBefore even thinking about depositing a single real dollar, your bot must pass this test:\n* **Run live paper trading for 30 to 90 days**.\n* **Win Rate & Payoff**: Achieve a positive expected value ($EV > 0$) after all exchange fees.\n* **Drawdown**: Never breach the **15% Handbrake circuit breaker**.\n* **Alpha**: Must perform better than simply holding Bitcoin in a spot wallet.\n\n---\n\n### Ready for Step 1?\nWould you like me to connect **live public Binance / Bybit WebSocket streams** to your dashboard so it tracks real-time live crypto prices (BTC / SOL / ETH) with a realistic paper-trading wallet?","thinking":"Acknowledged the user's decision to pursue the automated trading path. This involves a simulation-first approach, using virtual funds with a test environment API. Crucially, the plan emphasizes realistic simulations by explicitly accounting for exchange fees, a critical factor for accurate profitability assessment.\n\n\nPath 4 emphasizes a risk-averse approach, requiring simulated trading with real-time market data before considering live capital. The simulation necessitates integration of live WebSocket feeds for accurate price data and the implementation of realistic fee and slippage models. This detailed simulation setup aims to ensure thorough performance evaluation under authentic market conditions.\n\n\n"}
